# F00 errata for review F00-attempt2 P3-1, P3-2, P3-4 (repair 3, A0 delegate, 2026-09-30)
# Raw lane logs are NOT rewritten (their sha256 stay as recorded in handoffs/F00.json); this file records how to read them.

[P3-1a] repair2/F00-SPOT-09_companion_json.log
  Recorded in inventory/handoff (attempt 2) as exit 0. The log itself shows `exit_code=1` for
  `find / -name PLAN_VALIDATION.json -not -path '/proc/*'`: -not -path filters output but does not prune,
  so find still descends /proc and exits 1 on permission-denied entries. Corrected: F00-SPOT-09 exit 1.
  Conclusion re-established by repair3/F00-SPOT-09b_plan_validation_pruned.log (pruned find, exit 0, no match).

[P3-1b] repo/trial_merges.log lines 17-18 and 264-265
  `abort_exit=0` is printed directly after "fatal: There is no merge to abort (MERGE_HEAD missing)".
  A real `git merge --abort` with no MERGE_HEAD returns 128 (A6 re-run, review F00-attempt2 recheck #11).
  The lane's trial-merge script was not preserved, so the capture bug cannot be confirmed; hypothesis:
  $? was taken after a pipe or `|| true`. Affects only the two trials with no merge state
  (codex <- add-ask-bill "already up to date"; main <- octopus refused). Merge exit codes and clean_after are unaffected.

[P3-1c] checks/*/12_test_e2e.log, checks/diag-main-filmdeps/D07_test_e2e.log, checks/guide/07_guide.log (line 5)
  `# env: ... PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=<unset>` is printed by checks/runner.sh:22 from the runner's own
  environment before the step's command string is evaluated. The step sets the variable inline
  (`# command=PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194/chrome-linux/chrome ...`, line 4;
  checks/pipeline.sh:36,39). The command line is authoritative; the header does not describe the step's environment.

